---
// Figure: the rebuild lock, step by step.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import './stampedes.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="st-lock-steps" title="A rebuild lock, step by step" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. Every Redis command and reply shown was observed on Redis 8.10.3. DELEX needs Redis 8.4 or later; earlier versions use the Lua script given below the figure.">
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <ol>
      <li>The copy of trending has just expired. Requests A and B arrive in different processes.</li>
      <li>A asks Redis for trending and misses.</li>
      <li>A takes the lock with SET lock:trending tok-A NX PX 5000; Redis replies OK.</li>
      <li>B also misses.</li>
      <li>B tries SET lock:trending tok-B NX PX 5000; the key exists, so Redis replies nil.</li>
      <li>B waits and polls GET about every 20 ms.</li>
      <li>A reads trending once more, in case another process stored a copy meanwhile; it is still missing.</li>
      <li>A runs the 200 ms query, the only one for this key.</li>
      <li>A stores the copy with SET … EX 60.</li>
      <li>A releases the lock with DELEX lock:trending IFEQ tok-A; Redis deletes it and replies 1.</li>
      <li>B's next GET is a hit. B waited about one rebuild; the database answered one query.</li>
    </ol>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { sequenceFigure } from '../shared/sequence.mjs';
  import { lockSpec } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="st-lock-steps"]').forEach(root => sequenceFigure(root, lockSpec));
</script>
